Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:42:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 00/10] OnePlus 11 (salami) mainline enablement

This series brings up the OnePlus 11 (codename "salami", SM8550) on
mainline Linux, on top of the v7.3 merge base c03c1a14507d.

Patches are grouped by function: appended-DTB boot support, the Samsung
AMB670YF07/YF08 DSI panel driver, the board device tree, a consolidated
salami_defconfig, touchscreen and hall sensor drivers, ath12k/PCIe WiFi
fixes, bootloader and TZ/HYP log readers, the qcom_battmgr ADSP fuel gauge
initialization, the IPA/modem cellular data path and eSIM GPIO support.

ynk (10):
  arm64: boot: Add support for appended device tree blob
  drm/panel: Add Samsung AMB670YF07/YF08 panel driver
  arm64: dts: qcom: Add OnePlus 11 (salami) device tree
  arm64: configs: salami: Add defconfig
  input: Add salami touchscreen and hall sensor drivers
  wifi: ath12k: fix WiFi bring-up and 5 GHz scanning on SM8550
  soc: qcom: add bootloader and TZ/HYP log readers
  power: supply: qcom_battmgr: initialize ADSP fuel gauge on OnePlus
    devices
  salami: enable cellular data path
  salami: add eSIM GPIO support

